### MEDUSA API — Challenge Flags & Submissions
### Run from VS Code REST Client. Use a local organizer/admin account.
### Ensure the competition is public and active, and team belongs to its organization.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@organizerEmail = organizer@example.com
@participantEmail = participant@example.com
@password = Replace-With-A-Long-Local-Test-Password
@organizationId = 1

### 1. Organizer login
# @name organizerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{organizerEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 2. Create a public test competition
# @name createSubmissionCompetition
POST {{baseUrl}}/competitions
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "organization_id": {{organizationId}},
  "name": "Submission Test CTF",
  "slug": "submission-test-ctf",
  "description": "Local challenge submission API test",
  "is_public": true
}

### 3. Publish competition
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/competitions/{{createSubmissionCompetition.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "published"
}

### 4. Create round
# @name createSubmissionRound
POST {{baseUrl}}/competitions/{{createSubmissionCompetition.response.body.$.id}}/rounds
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Submission Round",
  "slug": "submission-round",
  "position": 1
}

### 5. Create draft challenge
# @name createSubmissionChallenge
POST {{baseUrl}}/rounds/{{createSubmissionRound.response.body.$.id}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Beacon Trace",
  "slug": "beacon-trace",
  "description": "Identify the beacon in the supplied packet capture.",
  "category": "Forensics",
  "points": 200,
  "difficulty": "medium"
}

### 6. Set challenge flag (local testing only; never use real production flags here)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{createSubmissionChallenge.response.body.$.id}}/flag
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flag": "MEDUSA{replace_this_with_a_local_test_flag}"
}

### 7. Publish challenge
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{createSubmissionChallenge.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "published"
}

### 8. Move competition to active
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/competitions/{{createSubmissionCompetition.response.body.$.id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "active"
}

### 9. Participant login
# @name participantLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{participantEmail}}&password={{password}}

### 10. Create a team as the participant (use the existing organization ID)
# @name createSubmissionTeam
POST {{baseUrl}}/organizations/{{organizationId}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{participantLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Submission Test Team"
}

### 11. Submit an incorrect flag (expected correct=false)
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{createSubmissionChallenge.response.body.$.id}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{participantLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{createSubmissionTeam.response.body.$.id}},
  "flag": "MEDUSA{wrong_local_test_flag}"
}

### 12. Submit the correct local test flag (expected correct=true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{createSubmissionChallenge.response.body.$.id}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{participantLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{createSubmissionTeam.response.body.$.id}},
  "flag": "MEDUSA{replace_this_with_a_local_test_flag}"
}

### 13. Submit again after solve (expected 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{createSubmissionChallenge.response.body.$.id}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{participantLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team_id": {{createSubmissionTeam.response.body.$.id}},
  "flag": "MEDUSA{replace_this_with_a_local_test_flag}"
}
